doc:sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "24AA(7) Use of and sharing returnable items" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) To avoid doubt, this section does not limit any other law of the Commonwealth that: (a) requires or authorises the use of a document or other thing; or  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to returnable items for the ACC  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (b) requires or authorises the making available (however described) of a document or other thing. Sharing returnable item for use by State, Territory or foreign agency" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24AA(8) Use of and sharing returnable items"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) The CEO may make a returnable item available to: (a) a State or Territory law enforcement agency; or (b) an agency that has responsibility for: (i) law enforcement in a foreign country; or (ii) intelligence gathering for a foreign country; or (iii) the security of a foreign country; to be used by that agency for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1), (5) or (6) and the purpose of any or all of the following (but not for any other purpose): (c) preventing, investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of a State or Territory; (d) proceedings under a corresponding law (within the meaning of the Proceeds of Crime Act 1987 or the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002); (e) proceedings for the forfeiture of the item under a law of a State or Territory; (f) deciding whether to institute proceedings or to take any other action mentioned in any of paragraphs 3ZQU(1)(a) to (l) (inclusive) of the Crimes Act 1914, subsection (5) or (6) of this section, or paragraph (c), (d) or (e) of this subsection. Ministerial arrangements for sharing" ;
    skos:definition "(8) The CEO may make a returnable item available to: (a) a State or Territory law enforcement agency; or (b) an agency that has responsibility for: (i) law enforcement in a foreign country; or (ii) intelligence gathering for a foreign country; or (iii) the security of a foreign country; to be used by that agency for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1), (5) or (6) and the purpose of any or all of the following (but not for any other purpose): (c) preventing, investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of a State or Territory; (d) proceedings under a corresponding law (within the meaning of the Proceeds of Crime Act 1987 or the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002); (e) proceedings for the forfeiture of the item under a law of a State or Territory; (f) deciding whether to institute proceedings or to take any other action mentioned in any of paragraphs 3ZQU(1)(a) to (l) (inclusive) of the Crimes Act 1914, subsection (5) or (6) of this section, or paragraph (c), (d) or (e) of this subsection. Ministerial arrangements for sharing"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7ca2ce51a66c6a07fd17960baea77510cb9042e22ef13eef037da3e520f4e9d4" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Sharing of returnable items with certain agencies" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012.pdf> ;
