doc:sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-8 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "24AA(8) Use of and sharing returnable items" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(8) The CEO may make a returnable item available to: (a) a State or Territory law enforcement agency; or (b) an agency that has responsibility for: (i) law enforcement in a foreign country; or (ii) intelligence gathering for a foreign country; or (iii) the security of a foreign country; to be used by that agency for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1), (5) or (6) and the purpose of any or all of the following (but not for any other purpose): (c) preventing, investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of a State or Territory; (d) proceedings under a corresponding law (within the meaning of the Proceeds of Crime Act 1987 or the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002); (e) proceedings for the forfeiture of the item under a law of a State or Territory; (f) deciding whether to institute proceedings or to take any other action mentioned in any of paragraphs 3ZQU(1)(a) to (l) (inclusive) of the Crimes Act 1914, subsection (5) or (6) of this section, or paragraph (c), (d) or (e) of this subsection. Ministerial arrangements for sharing" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-9 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24AA(9) Use of and sharing returnable items"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-9 ;
    values:originalText "(9) This section does not prevent the Minister from making an arrangement with a Minister of a State or Territory for: (a) the making available to a State or Territory law enforcement agency of that State or Territory, for purposes mentioned in subsections (1), (6) and (8), of returnable items; and (b) the disposal by the agency of such items when they are no longer of use to that agency for those purposes. Note: This subsection does not empower the Minister to make such an arrangement.  Amendments relating to returnable items for the ACC  Schedule 3  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 24AB  When returnable items must be returned" ;
    skos:definition "(9) This section does not prevent the Minister from making an arrangement with a Minister of a State or Territory for: (a) the making available to a State or Territory law enforcement agency of that State or Territory, for purposes mentioned in subsections (1), (6) and (8), of returnable items; and (b) the disposal by the agency of such items when they are no longer of use to that agency for those purposes. Note: This subsection does not empower the Minister to make such an arrangement.  Amendments relating to returnable items for the ACC  Schedule 3  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 24AB  When returnable items must be returned"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a194422aedc132876b908d214f835feb84b5f1e773681813ffc74118fbde4d7" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Permits sharing of returnable items with State or Territory law enforcement agencies." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
