concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24AA(1) Use of and sharing returnable items"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the CEO is satisfied that a returnable item is not required (or is no longer required) for a purpose mentioned in section 24AA or for other judicial or administrative review proceedings, the CEO must take reasonable steps to return the item to: (a) the person from whom the item was seized, or the person who produced the item; or (b) the owner, if the person mentioned in paragraph (a) is not entitled to possess it." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the CEO is satisfied that a returnable item is not required (or is no longer required) for a purpose mentioned in section 24AA or for other judicial or administrative review proceedings, the CEO must take reasonable steps to return the item to: (a) the person from whom the item was seized, or the person who produced the item; or (b) the owner, if the person mentioned in paragraph (a) is not entitled to possess it."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eb420f4eb5415197bc994cd4c3e4c08fabe85895867cbd7a497f3d7cdc12f74b" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "CEO may make returnable item available to constable or Commonwealth officer for specified purposes. Return a returnable item to the person from whom it was seized or produced if not required for judicial review proceedings." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
