doc:sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "24AA(1) Use of and sharing returnable items" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the CEO is satisfied that a returnable item is not required (or is no longer required) for a purpose mentioned in section 24AA or for other judicial or administrative review proceedings, the CEO must take reasonable steps to return the item to: (a) the person from whom the item was seized, or the person who produced the item; or (b) the owner, if the person mentioned in paragraph (a) is not entitled to possess it." ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24AA(2) Use of and sharing returnable items"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-24aa-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, the CEO does not have to take those steps if: (a) either: (i) the returnable item may be retained because of an order under subsection 24AC(2), or any other order under that subsection has been made in relation to the item; or (ii) the CEO has applied for such an order and the application has not been determined; or (b) the returnable item may otherwise be retained, destroyed or disposed of under a law, or an order of a court or tribunal, of the Commonwealth or of a State or a Territory; or (c) the returnable item is forfeited or forfeitable to the Commonwealth or is the subject of a dispute as to ownership." ;
    skos:definition "(2) However, the CEO does not have to take those steps if: (a) either: (i) the returnable item may be retained because of an order under subsection 24AC(2), or any other order under that subsection has been made in relation to the item; or (ii) the CEO has applied for such an order and the application has not been determined; or (b) the returnable item may otherwise be retained, destroyed or disposed of under a law, or an order of a court or tribunal, of the Commonwealth or of a State or a Territory; or (c) the returnable item is forfeited or forfeitable to the Commonwealth or is the subject of a dispute as to ownership."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a4b6cdf2bae08b4619c493ffe802a33e6d092ce76826bc8c091e4de5d6bebb2c" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-3-sec-24aa ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Use of returnable items by non-staff members is permitted. No obligation to take steps if certain conditions are met." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012.pdf, p.36" ;
