concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-77a-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "77A(4) Disclosure of notice may be prohibited"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-77a-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The Integrity Commissioner may include a notation in the notice if the Integrity Commissioner is satisfied that: (a) failure to do so might prejudice: (i) a person’s safety or reputation; or (ii) the fair trial of a person who has been, or may be, charged with an offence; or (iii) the investigation to which the notice relates or another corruption investigation; or (iv) any action taken as a result of an investigation referred to in subparagraph (iii); or (b) failure to do so might otherwise be contrary to the public interest." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The Integrity Commissioner may include a notation in the notice if the Integrity Commissioner is satisfied that: (a) failure to do so might prejudice: (i) a person’s safety or reputation; or (ii) the fair trial of a person who has been, or may be, charged with an offence; or (iii) the investigation to which the notice relates or another corruption investigation; or (iv) any action taken as a result of an investigation referred to in subparagraph (iii); or (b) failure to do so might otherwise be contrary to the public interest."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0bf8116b632b1e422c67f1f053948e5045c1da2fd9f3a1e8a05658bb0040180b" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-77a ;
