doc:sch-4-sec-77b-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "77B(5) Offences of disclosure" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) A person commits an offence if: (a) a disclosure is made to a person about: (i) a notice under section 75 that includes a notation under section 77A; or (ii) any official matter connected with a notice under section 75 that includes a notation under section 77A; and (b) the disclosure is permitted under subsection (2) or (4) because the person is a person of a particular kind; and (c) when the person is no longer a person of that kind, the person: (i) makes a record of the notice; or (ii) discloses the existence of the notice; or (iii) discloses any information about the notice or the existence of it; and (d) when the record, or disclosure, is made by the person: (i) the notation has not been cancelled by subsection 77A(7); and (ii) the period of 5 years after the notice is served under section 75 has not ended. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months." ;
