concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-77b-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "77B(6) Offences of disclosure"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-77b-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) A reference in this section to disclosing something’s existence includes disclosing information from which a person could reasonably be expected to infer its existence.  Schedule 4  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012" ;
    skos:definition "(6) A reference in this section to disclosing something’s existence includes disclosing information from which a person could reasonably be expected to infer its existence.  Schedule 4  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "866e05897e42fa09b9389aa109f56edf4ed37ce76d61e4e4193128e6c027ad46" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-77b ;
    cof:pageNumber "47"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosing information that could reasonably be expected to infer the existence of something is prohibited." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
