concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-14 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14 Subsection 79(5)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-14 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (5) If a legal practitioner gets agreement, as mentioned in subsection (3): (a) the fact that he or she: (i) gives information; or (ii) produces a document or thing; does not otherwise affect a claim of legal professional privilege that anyone may make in relation to that information, document or thing; and (b) the information or document does not cease to be the subject of legal professional privilege merely because it is given, produced or referred to." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (5) If a legal practitioner gets agreement, as mentioned in subsection (3): (a) the fact that he or she: (i) gives information; or (ii) produces a document or thing; does not otherwise affect a claim of legal professional privilege that anyone may make in relation to that information, document or thing; and (b) the information or document does not cease to be the subject of legal professional privilege merely because it is given, produced or referred to."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66a2360872107061bc3491cbd23c177d796ff1e8644de47a2de1541451247aeb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Legal professional privilege does not affect information or document given, produced, or referred to." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
