    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (5) If a legal practitioner gets agreement, as mentioned in subsection (3): (a) the fact that he or she: (i) gives information; or (ii) produces a document or thing; does not otherwise affect a claim of legal professional privilege that anyone may make in relation to that information, document or thing; and (b) the information or document does not cease to be the subject of legal professional privilege merely because it is given, produced or referred to." ;
