concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96B(6) Federal Court or Supreme Court to deal with contempt"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-96b-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If, after: (a) considering the matters specified in the certificate; and (b) hearing or receiving any evidence or statements by or in support of ACLEI; and (c) hearing or receiving any evidence or statements by or in support of the person; the court to which the application was made finds that the person was in contempt of ACLEI, the court may deal with the person as if the acts or omissions involved constituted a contempt of that court." ;
    skos:definition "(6) If, after: (a) considering the matters specified in the certificate; and (b) hearing or receiving any evidence or statements by or in support of ACLEI; and (c) hearing or receiving any evidence or statements by or in support of the person; the court to which the application was made finds that the person was in contempt of ACLEI, the court may deal with the person as if the acts or omissions involved constituted a contempt of that court."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "01662d2116f8c541afb0d00a47cbadb16b19e0acb7b8b4343b79a07157deb3d4" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96b ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may deal with person as if acts or omissions constituted contempt of court." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012.pdf> ;
