concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96B(7) Federal Court or Supreme Court to deal with contempt"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-96b-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) For the purposes of determining whether a person is in contempt of ACLEI under subsection (1), Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code applies as if: (a) being in contempt of ACLEI were an offence; and (b) references to a person being criminally responsible for an offence were references to a person being responsible for being in contempt of ACLEI.  Schedule 4  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012" ;
    skos:definition "(7) For the purposes of determining whether a person is in contempt of ACLEI under subsection (1), Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code applies as if: (a) being in contempt of ACLEI were an offence; and (b) references to a person being criminally responsible for an offence were references to a person being responsible for being in contempt of ACLEI.  Schedule 4  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4fcaefffa17f43981dc98781e001f10a28fad2ca509312c255869fe5f4d1d6fc" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96b ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Federal Court or Supreme Court to deal with contempt" ;
