concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96d-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96D(4) Person in contempt may be detained"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-96d-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The court may also impose any other condition on the release, for example: (a) that the person surrender his or her passport; or  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (b) that the person give an undertaking as to his or her living arrangements; or (c) that the person report as required to: (i) the AFP; or (ii) a police force or police service of a State; or (iii) any other authority or person responsible for the enforcement of the laws of the Commonwealth or of the States." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The court may also impose any other condition on the release, for example: (a) that the person surrender his or her passport; or  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (b) that the person give an undertaking as to his or her living arrangements; or (c) that the person report as required to: (i) the AFP; or (ii) a police force or police service of a State; or (iii) any other authority or person responsible for the enforcement of the laws of the Commonwealth or of the States."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b85b32f78ae3f3a7f18f1dcd5dca473ddf4bf7188fe9079562ef43b0d6675c88" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96d ;
    cof:pageNumber "56"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The court may impose conditions on the release of a person in contempt." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
