    cof:title "96E(2) Integrity Commissioner may withdraw contempt application" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If: (a) the Integrity Commissioner does so; and (b) the person to whom the application relates is in detention under section 96D; the person must be released from detention immediately." ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96F Double jeopardy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-96f ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an act or omission by a person is an offence against this Act and is also an offence against a law of a State, the person may be prosecuted and convicted under this Act or under that law of that State in respect of the act or omission, but nothing in this Act renders a person liable to be punished twice in respect of the same act or omission. (2) If: (a) an application is made to the Federal Court or a Supreme Court under subsection 96B(1) in respect of an act or omission by a person; and (b) the person is dealt with by the court under that section in respect of the act or omission;  Schedule 4  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 the person is not liable to be prosecuted for an offence in respect of that act or omission. (3) If a person is prosecuted for an offence in respect of an act or omission referred to in subsection 96A(1) without an application being made to the Federal Court or a Supreme Court under subsection 96B(1) in respect of the act or omission, an application must not be made under subsection 96B(1) in respect of the act or omission." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an act or omission by a person is an offence against this Act and is also an offence against a law of a State, the person may be prosecuted and convicted under this Act or under that law of that State in respect of the act or omission, but nothing in this Act renders a person liable to be punished twice in respect of the same act or omission. (2) If: (a) an application is made to the Federal Court or a Supreme Court under subsection 96B(1) in respect of an act or omission by a person; and (b) the person is dealt with by the court under that section in respect of the act or omission;  Schedule 4  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 the person is not liable to be prosecuted for an offence in respect of that act or omission. (3) If a person is prosecuted for an offence in respect of an act or omission referred to in subsection 96A(1) without an application being made to the Federal Court or a Supreme Court under subsection 96B(1) in respect of the act or omission, an application must not be made under subsection 96B(1) in respect of the act or omission."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8cace68cd125a7cb5cdab34391ab4fbd479169b86fe2a3ad97010f153db87aa9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96f-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96f-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96f-ss-3 ;
