concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32 Subsection 99(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-32 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute: (1) An authorised officer may apply to a Judge of the Federal Court or of the Supreme Court of a State or Territory for a warrant to arrest a person if: (a) both of the following apply: (i) the person has been ordered to deliver his or her passport to the Integrity Commissioner (whether or not the person has complied with the order); (ii) the authorised officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person is likely to leave Australia for the purpose of avoiding giving evidence at a hearing before the Integrity Commissioner; or (b) the person is to be served with a summons under section 83 and the authorised officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person: (i) has absconded or is likely to abscond; or  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (ii) is otherwise attempting, or likely to attempt, to evade service of the summons; or (c) the authorised officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under subsection 93(1) or is likely to do so." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute: (1) An authorised officer may apply to a Judge of the Federal Court or of the Supreme Court of a State or Territory for a warrant to arrest a person if: (a) both of the following apply: (i) the person has been ordered to deliver his or her passport to the Integrity Commissioner (whether or not the person has complied with the order); (ii) the authorised officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person is likely to leave Australia for the purpose of avoiding giving evidence at a hearing before the Integrity Commissioner; or (b) the person is to be served with a summons under section 83 and the authorised officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person: (i) has absconded or is likely to abscond; or  Amendments relating to the Integrity Commissioner’s investigative powers  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers and Offences) Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/04/2012 (ii) is otherwise attempting, or likely to attempt, to evade service of the summons; or (c) the authorised officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person has committed an offence under subsection 93(1) or is likely to do so."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bab400491213f1238bd5ca5b36b7622a96460e3db3adb611963fd44884d4384a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorized officer may apply for warrant to arrest person if they have not complied with order or are likely to leave Australia to avoid giving evidence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012.pdf, p.58" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32-norm .
