concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-and-offences-act-2012-sch-7-sec-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 Subsection 16(1) (definition of supervision period)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-5 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the definition, substitute: supervision period, in relation to a person who is released on parole or on licence, means the period: (a) starting when the person is released from prison on parole or licence; and (b) ending at the earlier of the following times: (i) the end of the person’s parole period or licence period; (ii) if the parole order or licence specifies an earlier time at which the supervision period is to end—that earlier time." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the definition, substitute: supervision period, in relation to a person who is released on parole or on licence, means the period: (a) starting when the person is released from prison on parole or licence; and (b) ending at the earlier of the following times: (i) the end of the person’s parole period or licence period; (ii) if the parole order or licence specifies an earlier time at which the supervision period is to end—that earlier time."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "90eedae892206eae22962039dda9973d6da084f0457bd846f4a501f3ad5c83b6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "72"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines supervision period for a person released on parole or licence." ;
